      "No. A visitor may drive any type of small vehicle listed on their full, valid driving licence - issued anywhere in the world - for 12 months from the date they last entered Great Britain, and nothing in British law requires an International Driving Permit alongside it. The only practical reason to carry one is a rental company that cannot read a licence in a non-Latin script and asks for a translation as a condition of the booking."
